                        "entry_id": "8869a5e3-2a31-364f-b991-6381fbb4b143",
                        "glosses": [
                            "in intuitionistic logic, a proposition P is decidable in a given theory if it can be proven from the theory that \\\"either P or not P\\\", i.e. in symbols: P∨¬P."
                        ],
